    "turn_text": "no i think you're absolutely right that One of a number of things that are just kind of horrendous about this now law. And they, because there are good reasons to, in my opinion, to incur additional debt when you're actually investing it in things that, over the long term, will help the society be more productive and will make people be more productive. But basically to give tax cuts to corporations, which I think every expert says will not result in significant growth in the economy, is the wrong way to do it. And there's so many things you could have done with that $1.5 trillion. We could have rebuilt every defective bridge in the country. We could have paid off everybody's student loans. We could have paid for community college for virtually everybody who wanted it. So again, if you're going to incur additional debt, make it so that there is a return on that investment later on. And I don't think there'll be any return from this or minimal return",
